.TH SANCHALA-BACKUP 1 "August 2026" "Sanchala OS" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
sanchala-backup \- Time Machine-like backup tool for Sanchala OS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sanchala-backup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sanchala-backup
provides snapshot management and backup functionality using Btrfs
snapshots via Snapper, with optional remote backup via Restic and
cloud sync via Rclone.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
List all snapshots for the specified config
.TP
.B create \fI[DESCRIPTION]\fR
Create a new manual snapshot
.TP
.B delete \fIID\fR
Delete a snapshot
.TP
.B info \fIID\fR
Show detailed snapshot information
.TP
.B compare \fIID1 ID2\fR
Compare two snapshots
.TP
.B browse \fIID\fR [\fIPATH\fR]
Browse snapshot contents
.TP
.B restore \fIID PATH\fR
Restore file or directory from snapshot
.TP
.B rollback \fIID\fR
Schedule full system rollback (requires reboot)
.TP
.B remote \fIACTION\fR
Manage remote backups (list, add, backup, status)
.TP
.B cloud \fIACTION\fR
Manage cloud sync (setup, sync, status)
.TP
.B status
Show backup system status
.TP
.B cleanup
Clean old snapshots
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-c, \-\-config \fINAME\fR
Snapper config to use (default: root)
.TP
.B \-\-json
Output in JSON format
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show help message
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a snapshot before making changes:
.B sanchala-backup create "Before config update"
.TP
Restore a file from snapshot 42:
.B sudo sanchala-backup restore 42 /etc/fstab
.TP
Full system rollback:
.B sudo sanchala-backup rollback 35
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sanchala/backup.toml
Main configuration file
.TP
.I /etc/snapper/configs/
Snapper configuration files
.TP
.I /.snapshots/
Snapshot storage directory
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR snapper (8),
.BR btrfs (8),
.BR restic (1),
.BR rclone (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Sanchala OS Team <dev@sanchala.id>
